// ICO - Hello World! :: RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   colour     : not assigned by Linguist
//   layer      : full (byte-balanced rainbow bar)
//   upstream   : https://github.com/quxianp/RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   reference  : see https://esolangs.org/ and https://rosettacode.org/

// ICO: a six-byte directory -- reserved, type, count -- and then
// one sixteen-byte entry per image.
//
// The entry describes the image with two 32-bit fields into this
// same file: its size and its offset. Both have to be right, or the
// reader lands somewhere random and reports a corrupt icon. The
// image itself here is the PNG above, which is the usual case since
// Vista and one format covers every size.
//
// There is no name and no comment in the format, so `Hello World!`
// is in this comment rather than in a field the reader would
// discard -- and it is in the embedded PNG too, in a tEXt chunk.
//
// ico: 126 bytes, dumped sixteen at a time.
//
// The bytes below are not hand-written. They are built from the
// format's own field widths by scripts/build_object_formats.py, and
// scripts/verify_encodings.py reads the fields back by name -- the
// magic number, the lengths, the offsets. A hex dump written from
// memory is wrong in one byte and looks exactly like a correct one.
//

// 00 00 01 00 01 00 01 01 00 00 01 00 20 00 68 00 |............ .h.|   <- 0000
// 00 00 16 00 00 00 89 50 4E 47 0D 0A 1A 0A 00 00 |.......PNG......|   <- 0010
// 00 0D 49 48 44 52 00 00 00 01 00 00 00 01 08 02 |..IHDR..........|   <- 0020
// 00 00 00 90 77 53 DE 00 00 00 18 74 45 58 74 44 |....wS.....tEXtD|   <- 0030
// 65 73 63 72 69 70 74 69 6F 6E 00 48 65 6C 6C 6F |escription.Hello|   <- 0040
// 20 57 6F 72 6C 64 21 5D CC 10 C2 00 00 00 0B 49 | World!].......I|   <- 0050
// 44 41 54 78 9C 63 60 00 02 00 00 05 00 01 7A 5E |DATx.c`.......z^|   <- 0060
// AB 3F 00 00 00 00 49 45 4E 44 AE 42 60 82       |.?....IEND.B`.|   <- 0070
